Commit the generated protobuf code instead of running protoc

The library's wire types are generated from the .proto files in
src/proto_src by prost-build, which upstream runs from build.rs on every
build. That needs `protoc`, the protobuf compiler, on the build host; the
Sailfish SDK build of the phone package has none, and a build script that
runs a host tool is one more thing to trust at build time.

The four generated files are committed in src/proto/ and included from
there; build.rs and the prost-build build dependency go. The files are
byte for byte what prost-build 0.13.5 (with libprotoc 3.21.12) emits for
the unchanged .proto files, so the types, and the wire format, are
exactly upstream's. The comment in lib.rs says how to regenerate them.

Findings: none; build (spec §3: the phone build has no protoc).
